===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|typography}}{{lb|en|typography}} ''Any of the following symbols:'' [[‒]] ({{l|en|figure dash}}), [[–]] ({{l|en|en dash}}), [[—]] ({{l|en|em dash}}), or [[―]] ({{l|en|horizontal bar}}).
#: {{hypo|en|Thesaurus:dash}}
#: {{hyper|en|Thesaurus:punctuation mark}}
## {{lb|en|computing}} A [[hyphen]] or [[minus sign]].
# {{lb|en|by extension}} The longer of the two symbols of [[Morse code]].
# A short [[run]], [[flight]].
#: {{syn|en|rush|sprint}}
#: {{uxi|en|When the feds came they did the '''dash'''.}}
# A rushing or violent onset.
#: {{syn|en|spurt|surge|thrust}}
# Violent [[strike]]; a [[whack]].
#: {{syn|en|blow|knock|thwack}}
#* {{quote-song|en|artist=C1 from LTH|title=Irrelevant Things|date=2018-01-24
|passage=They say that I’m way too cold, I never get tired of rappin<br/>My word is bang where I come from<br/>Watch be one work is magic</br>Do it and dash it<br/>Smile on MAT</br>No way this peng one acting<br/>Who got whacked and who got slapped<br/>And who got spared by '''dashes'''}}
# A small [[quantity]] of a [[liquid]] substance etc.; less than 1/8 of a [[teaspoon]].
#: {{syn|en|drop|skoosh|soupçon|Thesaurus:modicum}}
#: {{ux|en|Add a '''dash''' of vinegar.}}
# {{lb|en|figurative|by extension}} A slight [[admixture]].
#: {{syn|en|element|hint|touch}}
#: {{ux|en|There is a '''dash''' of craziness in his personality.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} {{U|ostentatious}} [[vigor]].
#: {{syn|en|energy|vim|vitality}}
#: {{ux|en|Aren't we full of '''dash''' this morning?}}
# {{lb|en|Nigeria|Ghana|Liberia|countable|uncountable}} A [[bribe]] or [[gratuity]]; a [[gift]].
#: {{syn|en|douceur|sweetener|Thesaurus:bribe|Thesaurus:gift}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The Abolition of the Slave Trade in Southeastern Nigeria, 1885{{ndash}}1950|passage=Writing in 1924 on a similar situation in Ugep, the political officer, Mr. S. T. Harvey noted: "In the old days there was no specified dowry but merely '''dashes''' given to the father-in-law, from 8 to 20 rods according to the status of the man{{...}}The dowry is made small because whatsoever a woman farms or reaps during her life time is by native custom the property of her parents."|year=2006|author=Adiele Eberechukwu Afigbo|page=99|isbn=978-1-58046-242-6|series=Rochester Studies in African History and the Diaspora|seriesvolume=25|issn=1092-5228|publisher=University of Rochester Press}}
# {{lb|en|dated|euphemistic}} {{n-g|A stand-in for a censored word, like "[[Devil]]" or "[[damn]]". (Compare [[deuce]].)}}
#: {{syn|en|beep|blankety-blank}}
#* '''1853''', {{w|William Makepeace Thackeray}}, ''{{w|The Newcomes}}'', Chapter VI, serialized in ''Harper's New Monthly Magazine'', (VIII, no. 43, Dec 1853) [http://books.google.com/books?id=WEFGAAAAcAAJ&dq=%22what%20the%20dash%22&pg=PA118#v=onepage&q=%22what%20the%20dash%22&f=true p. 118]
# {{ellipsis of|en|dashboard}}.
#: {{syn|en|control panel|instrument panel}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=October 19 1955|author=w:Rex Stout|title=The Next Witness|page=31|publisher=[[w:Three Witnesses (book)|''Three Witnesses'']], 94 [[w:Bantam Books|Bantam]]|isbn=0553249592
|passage=The '''dash''' clock said 2:38 when{{...}} I turned off a dirt road{{...}}.}}
## {{lb|en|Internet|informal}} The [[dashboard]] of a [[social media]] user.
##: {{syn|en|timeline|feed|graphical user interface}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=2018|author=Krista Ritchie; Becca Ritchie|title=Alphas Like Us|pageurl=https://www.google.com/books/edition/Alphas_Like_Us/4uD5DwAAQBAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=%22my+dash%22+tumblr&pg=PT178&printsec=frontcover|page=unnumbered
|passage=“You wanna know what else is all over my '''dash'''? Gifs of you and your boyfriend."}}
##* {{see more citations|en}}
# {{lb|en|UK|India}} A prime symbol.

